---
// Three steps from a day-to-day complaint to a feature, as an illustrative
// example. The words are invented for this page: the quote is not a real quote
// from anyone, and the feature is not a description of any real feature. The
// quotation is not attributed.
//
// Real HTML, so axe can check the contrast. The last step is in the accent.
// Side by side from 40rem, stacked below that.
---

<figure class="p2f">
  <p class="illus-tag">Illustrative example: not a real quote or a real feature description</p>
  <ol class="p2f__steps">
    <li class="p2f__step">
      <p class="p2f__head">What someone says</p>
      <blockquote class="p2f__quote">
        <p>&ldquo;I only find out a proof is late when the customer rings.&rdquo;</p>
      </blockquote>
    </li>
    <li class="p2f__step">
      <p class="p2f__head">What’s really wrong</p>
      <p class="p2f__line">A late proof isn’t visible to anyone until it’s too late.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="p2f__step p2f__step--fix">
      <p class="p2f__head">A feature that fixes it</p>
      <p class="p2f__line">An alert when a proof has waited too long.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</figure>
